  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-RAD-05 and RBC-LAB-03. I checked each patient by name, date of birth and MRN. 12 of 13 items are closed. One is left open on purpose.\n\nOriginal 8 items:\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram 10/19: no cause found for the hematuria. It showed a 4 mm LLL nodule that his lung screening program already follows. I ordered the next screening LDCT on the 12-month schedule (sr-t0001), set a tracking task (task-t0002), messaged him and wrote a note. This was changed later (see below).\n- pt-0016, TSH 2.1: normal, closed.\n- pt-0016, potassium: the lab corrected the 6.3 to 4.4 (analyzer error). Normal, closed with no action.\n- pt-0007, preliminary CTA chest: I used the final report (dr-00084). It found no PE and no nodule (the \"nodule\" was a vessel) and says no lung follow-up is needed. Closed.\n- pt-0064, creatinine 1.36 from 9/26: does not count as acute kidney injury (AKI) because there was no earlier creatinine within 7 days. No action.\n- pt-0007, BMP 10/22: AKI, creatinine 1.64 vs 0.98 about 35 hours earlier. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by Mon 10/26 (sr-t0010), sent the patient an urgent message and wrote a note.\n- pt-0033, BMP 10/22: creatinine 1.31 is not AKI. I left out the 10/21 value because it was entered in error; the lowest value in the prior 7 days was 1.27. No action.\n- pt-0008 Walter Brennan, potassium 6.4: at first it was flagged hemolyzed. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0015) and messaged him (this was replaced, see below).\n\nNew items that came in while I was working:\n- pt-0008: the lab withdrew the hemolysis flag, so the 6.4 is real. I switched to the stat pathway: messaged on-call at stat priority, ordered a stat BMP for today (sr-t0019) and sent him a corrected message to come in today. His medication list has no ACE inhibitor, ARB, spironolactone-type drug, potassium supplement or NSAID. I did not hold metoprolol because stopping it suddenly is unsafe with his heart disease. Note written.\n- pt-0033: a new outside creatinine of 1.78 is AKI (up from 1.31 nine hours earlier). I ordered an urgent BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0025), sent an urgent message and wrote a note.\n- pt-0064: a new creatinine of 1.48 is not AKI (no earlier value within 7 days). No action.\n- pt-0006: an addendum from the screening program changes his April LDCT to Lung-RADS 3 (probably benign) because of a new 5 mm RUL nodule, and asks for a repeat LDCT at 6 months. That is a window of 9/14–11/14. I ordered the LDCT for now through 11/14 (sr-t0030), set a tracking task due 11/14 (task-t0031), sent him a corrected message and wrote a note.\n\nNeeds your action:\n- **Two orders need cancelling by hand.** My tools can't cancel lab or imaging orders, and they wouldn't let me cancel tracking tasks I created myself. So these are still active, each with a task asking you to cancel it:\n  - sr-t0015 (pt-0008's urgent BMP, replaced by the stat one): task-t0022.\n  - sr-t0001 and its tracking task task-t0002 (pt-0006's 12-month LDCT): task-t0032.\n\nLeft open:\n- inbox-a0002, pt-0007 preliminary chest X-ray 10/22 (possible 7 mm RUL opacity): no final report yet, so it stays open under §2(c).\n- Not touched: 6 refill messages in your messages queue (pt-0030, pt-0027, pt-0031). They came in before I started and are outside the results inbox.",
